# Arco Group of Companies — the white-label brand for the web app.
#
#   Docker:        docker run --env-file brands/arco.env -e AGENT_URL=http://agent:3001 -p 8080:80 rafai-web
#   Dev / static:  cp brands/arco.env .env.local && npm run dev        (or: npm run build)
#
# The images are files in brands/arco/, named below by their path on the site.
# A build, or the container at start, copies in only the files named here, so
# this customer's site serves its own logo and no one else's. source.png is the
# artwork as supplied; logo.png is it trimmed to 144 px tall at most, twice the
# sidebar's 72 px; icon.png is the tab icon. All are transparent.
#
# Colours are taken from the logo. Its blue (#0685d3) is 3.8:1 against the page,
# under the 4.5:1 the accent needs as text, so the accent is that blue a shade
# deeper (#0575ba); on the dark theme it is 4.4:1, so a shade lighter (#068ada).
# The bar across the top is the logo's own blue, and the sidebar is left
# neutral. The white ring and lettering are transparent in the artwork — right
# on the light page, black on the dark one — so logo-dark.png puts the white
# back. The icon is the inner roundel.
#
# The assistant's OWN name — what it answers when asked who it is — is set on the
# agent service, as tenant "arco" in rafai-ai-agent/src/db/tenants.json.

BRAND_NAME=Arco AI
BRAND_COMPANY=Arco Group of Companies
BRAND_TAGLINE=Analytics
BRAND_ACCENT=0575ba
BRAND_ACCENT_DARK=068ada
BRAND_BAR=0685d3
BRAND_LOGO_URL=/brands/arco/logo.png
BRAND_LOGO_DARK_URL=/brands/arco/logo-dark.png
BRAND_FAVICON_URL=/brands/arco/icon.png
BRAND_SHARE_IMAGE_URL=/brands/arco/share.png
